<!-- cnic-policy.html -->
<!Doctype html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <title>CNIC Data Policy — Pickker.pk</title>
    <link rel="shortcut icon" href="/Imgs/logo.png" type="image/x-icon">
    <style>
        :root {
            --green: #0a7a3f;
            --dark: #083d25;
            --muted: #6b7280;
            --max: 900px
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box
        }

        body {
            font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Noto Nastaliq Urdu', sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            background: #f7faf7;
            color: #0f1724
        }

        .container {
            max-width: var(--max);
            margin: 32px auto;
            padding: 24px;
            background: #fff;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(2, 6, 23, 0.06)
        }

        header {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 12px
        }

        .logo {
            width: 54px;
            height: 54px;
            border-radius: 40px;
            background-image: url('logo.png');
            background-size: cover;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            color: #fff;
            font-weight: 700
        }

        h1 {
            margin: 8px 0 12px;
            font-size: 20px
        }

        p {
            color: var(--muted);
            line-height: 1.6
        }

        h2 {
            color: var(--dark);
            margin-top: 20px
        }

        .note {
            background: #f0fff6;
            border-left: 4px solid var(--green);
            padding: 12px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin: 12px 0
        }

        footer {
            margin-top: 28px;
            padding-top: 18px;
            border-top: 1px solid #eef2f7;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: space-between;
            align-items: center
        }

        a.btn {
            background: var(--green);
            color: #fff;
            padding: 8px 12px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            text-decoration: none
        }

        .muted {
            color: var(--muted);
            font-size: 13px
        }

        @media (max-width:600px) {
            .container {
                margin: 12px;
                padding: 16px
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>
    <div class="container">
        <header>
            <div class="logo"></div>
            <div>
                <strong>Pickker.pk</strong>
                <div class="muted">Pakistan ka apna marketplace</div>
            </div>
        </header>

        <h1>CNIC Data Policy</h1>
        <p><strong>Date: </strong>30/9/2025</p>

        <div class="note">
            <strong>Short summary:</strong> We collect CNIC images only to verify seller identity and reduce fraud. CNIC
            files are stored securely and retained for a limited time.
        </div>

        <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect CNIC front/back images, and optional selfie or short verification video when uploaded by a user
            for identity verification.</p>

        <h2>2. Purpose</h2>
        <p>To verify seller identity, reduce fraudulent listings, and improve safety of the marketplace. Verified users
            receive a CNIC Verified badge.</p>

        <h2>3. Storage &amp; Access</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>CNIC files are stored encrypted in our secure storage (S3 or equivalent).</li>
            <li>Only verification admins can access these files via a signed URL and every access is logged.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Retention</h2>
        <p>CNIC files are retained for <strong>90 days</strong> after verification and are then permanently deleted. We
            retain a masked CNIC (e.g., 42101-*****-1) and the verification record for audit.</p>

        <h2>5. User rights</h2>
        <p>Users may request deletion of their CNIC files at any time by contacting verification@Pickker.pk. Deleting
            CNIC data will remove verification status.</p>

        <h2>6. Sharing</h2>
        <p>We do not share CNIC files with third parties except when required by law or official requests from
            authorities.</p>

        <footer>
            <div class="muted">For CNIC data requests: verification@Pickker.pk</div>
        </footer>
    </div>
</body>

</html>